## TZ-236.C — PdfRender production-ready (C.1 backgrounds + C.2 async queue + C.3 header/footer) — DONE 2026-07-30

**Parent:** TZ-236W (PDF/Print стек — 4 waves, ~140-180h)
**Sub-TZ:** C (all 3 sub-waves in one commit)
**Commit:** ec54189 — 4 files changed, +355/-44 lines
**Sync commit:** ea3de11 (sync main bece1c42 with 3 conflict resolutions)
**Status:** ✅ DONE

### Mission
Advance PdfRender module from MVP (TZ-236.B) to production-ready state.
Three sub-waves implemented in single atomic commit.

### Sub-wave C.1 — Background images in PDF
**Problem:** Gotenberg (in Docker) cannot fetch template background images from host backend (relative `/uploads/*` URLs).

**Solution:** Add `extra_hosts: ["host.docker.internal:host-gateway"]` to docker-compose gotenberg service + regex rewrite `/uploads/*` URLs in HTML to absolute `BACKEND_PUBLIC_URL` (defaults to `http://host.docker.internal:3000`) before sending to Gotenberg.

**Files:**
- `docker-compose.yml` (modified — added extra_hosts block)
- `backend/src/modules/pdf-render/pdf-render.service.ts` (URL regex rewrite in `renderFromHtmlAndTemplate`)
- `backend/src/config/env.validation.ts` (added `BACKEND_PUBLIC_URL?: string`)

### Sub-wave C.2 — Async render queue (in-memory FIFO + TTL)
**Problem:** Sync rendering can hit 60s timeout for large templates (>50 blocks). Multiple simultaneous renders overwhelm Gotenberg.

**Solution:** In-memory FIFO queue with MAX_CONCURRENT=2 concurrency cap + per-job TTL of 1 hour + periodic GC.

**Files:**
- `backend/src/modules/pdf-render/pdf-render.service.ts`:
  - `jobs: Map<string, JobState>` — pending/processing/done/failed
  - `queue: Array<{jobId, templateId, dto}>` — FIFO
  - `activeRenders: number` — concurrency cap counter
  - `enqueueRender()` — returns jobId immediately (caller polls)
  - `processQueue()` — worker loop (FIFO + MAX_CONCURRENT)
  - `runJob()` — per-job render execution
  - `gcStaleJobs()` — periodic cleanup of jobs older than JOB_TTL_MS
  - `setInterval(..., 5min).unref()` — GC interval (doesn't block shutdown)
- `backend/src/modules/pdf-render/pdf-render.controller.ts`:
  - NEW `POST /async/from-template/:templateId` (202 Accepted) → `{jobId, status}`
  - NEW `GET /jobs/:jobId` → status JSON
  - NEW `GET /jobs/:jobId/download` → consumes PDF buffer

**Backward compat:** Original `POST /from-template/:templateId` sync endpoint PRESERVED untouched.

### Sub-wave C.3 — Header/footer injection (Chromium API)
**Problem:** Documents need page numbering and template name in header/footer.

**Solution:** Use Chromium's native `--header-template` / `--footer-template` form fields with HTML containing Chromium placeholders (`class="pageNumber"`, `class="totalPages"`, `class="title"`, `class="date"`). Auto-bump `marginTop`/`marginBottom` when header/footer present.

**Files:**
- `backend/src/modules/pdf-render/pdf-render.service.ts`:
  - `buildDefaultHeader(template)` — `<span class="title">${template.name}</span> &middot; <span>${organizationId.slice(-6)}</span>`
  - `buildDefaultFooter(_template)` — `<span class="pageNumber"></span> / <span class="totalPages"></span> &middot; <span class="date"></span>`
  - `escapeHtml(s)` — minimal HTML escape for template.name (defense-in-depth)
  - `HF_MARGIN_INCHES = 0.79` (~20mm reserved for sticky zones)
- DTO supports optional `htmlHeader?` / `htmlFooter?` via TypeScript cast (future override hook, upgradeable to proper DTO field when override callers exist)

### Architecture summary
```
┌────────────────────────┐                            ┌─────────────────────┐
│ Sync flow (TZ-236.B):  │  POST /from-template/:id   │                     │
│ client ──request──►   │ ───────────────────────►  │  PdfRenderService   │
│ client ◄──PDF ◄────   │  (StreamableFile)         │  ↓ GET /api/...     │
└────────────────────────┘                            └─────────────────────┘
┌────────────────────────┐                            ┌─────────────────────┐
│ Async flow (TZ-236.C): │  POST /async/.../:id      │   jobs Map<jobId,   │
│ client ──jobId──►     │ ───────────────────────►  │   JobState>         │
│ client  poll ───────► │  GET /jobs/:jobId         │   (FIFO + concurrency│
│ client ──PDF ────►    │  GET /jobs/:jobId/download│    + TTL GC)        │
└────────────────────────┘                            └─────────────────────┘
                                                          │
                                                          ▼
                                                  ┌──────────────────┐
                                                  │ Gotenberg        │
                                                  │ Chromium headless│
                                                  │ (+ host.docker.   │
                                                  │  .internal for   │
                                                  │  backgrounds,    │
                                                  │  + HF margins)   │
                                                  └──────────────────┘
```

### Code review
- Reviewer APPROVE with 3 non-blocking notes (documented for future hardening):
  1. **renderHtml body padding regression risk** — `renderHtml` sets `body { padding: 20px }`. Combined with new `HF_MARGIN_INCHES=0.79` (=20mm) marginTop → ~37px top whitespace before content. Header sits in gotenberg's margin zone, body content below. Smoke-test on multi-page doc to confirm visual OK. If looks wrong, remove body padding or shrink HF margin.
  2. **`processQueue()` re-entrance** — `enqueueRender()` and `runJob().finally()` both call `void this.processQueue()`. `shift()` at top makes this safe (concurrency bounded by MAX_CONCURRENT=2), but log "queue depth=N" can show stale value during rapid enqueues. Add `isProcessing` flag in Round 4 hardening.
  3. **DTO `htmlHeader?`/`htmlFooter?` cast is brittle** — TypeScript-level cast works, but fields don't exist on class-validator schema → invisible to Swagger / future validation tightening. Promote to proper DTO optional fields when override callers materialize.

### Verification
- `cd backend && npx tsc --noEmit` → **0 errors** in pdf-render section.
- Module structure consistent (`generated-document.module.ts` is reference pattern).
- Native `fetch` + `FormData` + `Blob` + `AbortController` — no new dependencies.
- `Roles` + `AuditAction` decorators consistent.

### Honest disclosure
- **Sync endpoint 60s timeout** remains. Async queue helps but only 2 concurrent renders.
- **In-memory jobs** lost on backend restart (clients retry from scratch).
- **Linux production** may need different `extra_hosts` strategy (e.g., `network_mode: host`).
- **Visual smoke test** needed for header/footer margin combination (Defer if renderHtml padding: 20px proves problematic).

### Endpoints summary
| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/pdf-render/from-template/:id` | Sync render (TZ-236.B compat) — returns PDF stream |
| POST | `/api/pdf-render/async/from-template/:id` | Enqueue async job — 202 + `{jobId, status}` |
| GET  | `/api/pdf-render/jobs/:jobId` | Job status (pending/processing/done/failed) |
| GET  | `/api/pdf-render/jobs/:jobId/download` | Consume PDF buffer for completed job |

